  "id": "attentional-strategy",
  "term": "attentional strategy",
  "definition": "An attentional strategy is a habitual way of directing selective attention to certain kinds of information during perception or processing. In the source packet, it refers to how speakers tend to focus more on particular speech features, such as segments or tones, often reflecting patterns carried over from their dominant language.",
